🚀 Install IIS and Google Chrome on Azure Windows VM using Custom Data

This repository demonstrates how to automatically install IIS (Web Server) and Google Chrome on an Azure Windows Virtual Machine using Custom Data (User Data) during0 VM creation.

📌 Problem Statement
When creating a Windows VM in Azure, we want to:
Automatically install IIS Web Server
Install Google Chrome
Deploy a sample web page


🧠 Concept: Azure Custom Data (User Data)

Custom Data allows us to run scripts once at VM first boot.
Key Characteristics
Runs only once
Executes before first login
Best for initial configuration
Supports PowerShell scripts on Windows
Automatically Base64 encoded by Azure Portal
Do this at first boot, without manual login



